    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8cd43ea6_913cbe22",
        "filename": "cc/binary.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 443,
      "author": {
        "id": 1067098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-07T01:30:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are at least three options:\n- what I\u0027ve implemented here\n- separate functions for whether to create symlink and whether to install to bootstrap (i.e. what I implemented in PS2)\n- annotations (i.e. your suggestion)\n\nThe problem with annotations is that it is not sufficient for handling the case where hwaddress is not in SANITIZE_TARGET but libc is HWASANified (through manual editing of Android.bp). In this case we would end up installing the only copy of the runtime to /system/lib64/bootstrap and non-bootstrap processes won\u0027t be able to find it. To handle this case I went back to the PS2 approach with special casing for the case where the target is the HWASAN runtime and hwaddress is in SANITIZE_TARGET.",
      "parentUuid": "a06ad4ef_d5809955",
      "revId": "42b8eb3a54cbef297802be3775efca1ae2749a39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
